keep. But if I discard F4, it might be safe since others have discarded it.\n\nSafety: Discarding honors that have been discarded is safe. F4 discarded twice, so very safe. But discarding W6 or W7? W6 was discarded by next player, so safe. W7 not discarded recently? B7 discarded, but not W7. So W6 is safer.\n\nFor tile efficiency, discarding W7 might retain W6 for possible chow with W5/W8? But for Outside Hand, that chow wouldn't qualify unless it includes terminal (W1 or W9). W9 is already used in meld. So no.\n\nThus, I'll discard a simple tile that is safe and not useful for Outside Hand.\n\nChoice: Discard W7.\n\nReason: My hand has a terminal pung (W9), so aiming for Outside Hand is plausible, requiring all melds and pair to contain terminals or honors. W7 is a simple tile with no terminal in its potential chows (since W9 is separate), and keeping it does not contribute to Outside Hand. Discarding it maintains flexibility with B1/B2 for a terminal chow and retains honors for potential pungs. It is also relatively safe as W7 hasn't been discarded recently, but it's a middle tile with 4 copies left, moderate risk.\n\nFinal decision: Play W7.\n\nAnswer: Play W7"}
